From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Herman van Hazendonk <github.com@herrie.org>
Date: Tue, 20 Oct 2026 16:47:18 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] Honour "Keep inline downloads" again, through
 use_storage_optimizer

The account option KeepInlineDownloads used to set
tdlibParameters.enable_storage_optimizer. TDLib turned that parameter into
the use_storage_optimizer option, and since the move to setTdlibParameters
nothing sets it: the option is still offered but has no effect, and TDLib
keeps its default.

Set use_storage_optimizer from the account option right after the
parameters. setOption is allowed before authorization, and TDLib holds such
requests until the database is open, so it can go out straight away.

The test suite expects the setOption request that now follows
setTdlibParameters at every login, with the option off when
keep-inline-downloads is set.

This is the pull request as it stands after review, squashed; it takes in:
- 27c8af2 "Build the use_storage_optimizer option by its fields' names" (Mikhail T.)

Signed-off-by: Herman van Hazendonk <github.com@herrie.org>
Upstream-Status: Submitted [https://github.com/UnitedMarsupials/tdlib-purple/pull/33]
---
